1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,050
Every prediction market dies the same way.

2
00:00:03,050 --> 00:00:04,250
It opens empty.

3
00:00:04,250 --> 00:00:05,050
No price.

4
00:00:05,050 --> 00:00:05,850
No counterparty.

5
00:00:05,850 --> 00:00:09,050
The first trader finds nothing, and walks away.

6
00:00:09,050 --> 00:00:12,650
A fifteen-minute market does that ninety-six times a day.

7
00:00:12,650 --> 00:00:15,050
Nobody has solved the cold start.

8
00:00:16,350 --> 00:00:17,550
Converge ends it.

9
00:00:17,550 --> 00:00:19,550
We turn liquidity into infrastructure.

10
00:00:19,550 --> 00:00:21,950
Deposit once into a single vault.

11
00:00:21,950 --> 00:00:25,150
That vault makes the market in every round,

12
00:00:25,150 --> 00:00:28,350
on every asset, from the very first second.

13
00:00:28,350 --> 00:00:31,950
Liquidity providers earn from spreads, never from token emissions.

14
00:00:33,250 --> 00:00:37,650
But a vault that quotes on-chain gets hunted by faster traders.

15
00:00:37,650 --> 00:00:38,850
We measured it.

16
00:00:38,850 --> 00:00:42,050
Our first design lost eighty-eight dollars a day

17
00:00:42,050 --> 00:00:44,850
to a bot with a one-second lead.

18
00:00:44,850 --> 00:00:47,250
So we redesigned the market itself.

19
00:00:47,250 --> 00:00:49,650
Orders fill two seconds later, at

20
00:00:49,650 --> 00:00:52,050
the oracle's price for that second.

21
00:00:52,050 --> 00:00:56,050
Backtested on ninety-one days of real prices, that turns the

22
00:00:56,050 --> 00:01:00,050
loss into about fifty dollars a day, under pessimistic assumptions.

23
00:01:00,050 --> 00:01:03,650
It breaks if a rival leads by three seconds.

24
00:01:03,650 --> 00:01:05,650
We say that out loud.

25
00:01:06,950 --> 00:01:09,133
Now watch a brand-new user.

26
00:01:09,133 --> 00:01:10,006
Face ID.

27
00:01:10,006 --> 00:01:12,625
No seed phrase, no extension: Mera

28
00:01:12,625 --> 00:01:15,244
turns a passkey into the wallet.

29
00:01:15,244 --> 00:01:18,300
Add test money, tap Up, confirm once.

30
00:01:18,300 --> 00:01:20,046
The keeper fills it.

31
00:01:20,046 --> 00:01:23,102
Eighteen point seven seconds from landing page

32
00:01:23,102 --> 00:01:26,158
to a live bet, on Monad testnet.

33
00:01:26,158 --> 00:01:29,650
Ethereum, Bitcoin, MON: one vault quotes them all.

34
00:01:30,950 --> 00:01:32,950
This only works on Monad.

35
00:01:32,950 --> 00:01:35,350
A block every three hundred milliseconds.

36
00:01:35,350 --> 00:01:39,350
Serving a trade costs about a sixth of a cent.

37
00:01:39,350 --> 00:01:41,350
On Ethereum, about ten cents.

38
00:01:41,350 --> 00:01:44,150
Fifty-seven times cheaper, at today's gas prices.

39
00:01:45,450 --> 00:01:47,450
The whole stack is real.

40
00:01:47,450 --> 00:01:49,850
Chainlink CRE is the orchestration layer,

41
00:01:49,850 --> 00:01:52,250
and we've broadcast its reports on-chain.

42
00:01:52,250 --> 00:01:56,650
Each round's Up token becomes its own order book on Kuru.

43
00:01:56,650 --> 00:01:58,250
Envio indexes the history.

44
00:01:58,250 --> 00:02:00,650
Mera is the entire account layer.

45
00:02:01,950 --> 00:02:03,550
And it's a platform.

46
00:02:03,550 --> 00:02:06,750
Any Monad app can launch a market with

47
00:02:06,750 --> 00:02:09,550
instant depth: one call, under hard caps.

48
00:02:09,550 --> 00:02:12,350
Loss limits are enforced on-chain: one percent

49
00:02:12,350 --> 00:02:14,750
per market, eight percent in total.

50
00:02:14,750 --> 00:02:16,750
And users can always exit.

51
00:02:18,050 --> 00:02:20,696
The trades you just watched ran

52
00:02:20,696 --> 00:02:23,343
live on testnet, with test money.

53
00:02:23,343 --> 00:02:25,107
No outside users yet.

54
00:02:25,107 --> 00:02:26,871
We're telling you first.

55
00:02:26,871 --> 00:02:31,282
Ten phases built, with four hundred and twelve contract tests.

56
00:02:31,282 --> 00:02:35,252
Four things unlock mainnet: Chainlink Data Streams access, CRE

57
00:02:35,252 --> 00:02:39,221
deploy access, Kuru market-creation rights, and an external audit.

58
00:02:39,221 --> 00:02:39,662
Converge.

59
00:02:39,662 --> 00:02:42,750
A market maker for every short round.
